.TH REALPATH 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
realpath \- print the resolved absolute pathname
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B realpath
.I path
.RI [ path ]\ .\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B realpath
prints the canonicalized absolute pathname of each
.I path
operand, one per line: symbolic links are resolved, and
.B .
and
.B ..
components are removed. Multiple operands are processed in turn; a
failure on one operand does not stop the rest from being attempted.
.PP
No options are recognized.
.PP
Every
.I path
operand must currently exist; unlike some other implementations of
this utility,
.B realpath
does not accept a
.I path
whose final component is missing and return the resolved form of its
parent with that missing name appended \(em a nonexistent
.I path
is always an error, at any component.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I path
A pathname of an existing file, directory, or other filesystem entry.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every
.I path
operand was resolved and printed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
A
.I path
operand could not be resolved (for example, because some component of
it does not exist); the rest of the operands were still attempted.
Also used if writing a result to standard output failed.
.TP
.B 2
No
.I path
operand was given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR readlink (1),
.BR pwd (1),
.BR pathchk (1)
